failure_location.quote:
The goal is to find a nonsingular matrix $P \in \GL_n(\R)$ and nonnegative scalars $\alpha_1, \dots, \alpha_k \geq 0$ such that the scaled frame $\tilde x_i = \alpha_i P x_i$ satisfies 
\begin{align*}
    \norm{\tilde x_i}_2 &= \frac{n}{k} \quad (i = 1, \dots, k), \\
    \sum_{i=1}^k \tilde x_i \tilde x_i^\top &= I_n.
\end{align*}

